  "question": {
    "text": "On decreasing the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, the solubility of a sparingly soluble salt <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>MX</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of a weak acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>HX</mi><mo>)</mo></math> increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HX</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
